## Deviations

1. Could not require `yin.vm.completion-test`'s private
   `scoping-corpus`/`kitchen-sink`/`maker-program`/`conformance-corpus`
   (see Corpus section above): file box forbids editing that namespace to
   make them public. Coverage is unaffected per the argument above.
2. `store-normalization-test` dissocs `completion/ffi-pair-keys` from the
   store before normalizing (see Normalizer section): the plain `:type`-
   dispatch normalizer has no way to recognize a bare host handle map/
   object that carries no `:type` key of its own, so this exclusion lives
   in the test, not in `normalize` itself. If a later phase wants host-
   handle exclusion built into the normalizer proper, it needs its own
   design decision about what marks a value as a "host handle" in general
   (this VM's only current instances are the FFI pair, which
   `yin.vm.completion` already names).
3. Kondo and cljstyle were denied, not run (see above); no lint/format
   verification beyond the ASCII check and manual review against this
   repo's existing test-file conventions (blank lines between top-level
   forms, `#?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default)` catch idiom
